X('customs-clearance-process-india',[('Checklist before the cargo ships',['IEC active and the bank account linked to it.','HS code and duty confirmed in writing by your broker.','BIS, FSSAI, WPC or other permissions in hand where the product needs them.','Draft invoice, packing list and bill of lading checked against each other.','Free days with the line and the depot known, and transport booked.','Duty funds ready in the account used for payment.']),('In practice',['A clean consignment with advance filing often clears within a day or two of arrival. The ones that take weeks almost always had a problem that was visible in the documents before the cargo left the origin. That is why the best use of a broker is early, not after the ship arrives.'])])
X('what-is-a-freight-forwarder',[('Checklist for working with a forwarder',['Share a full packing list with weights and dimensions, not an estimate.','Confirm the Incoterm so both sides know who books and pays what.','Ask for the quote in writing with every charge shown.','Agree who handles origin and destination customs.','Ask for the cut-off dates and the documents needed for each.']),('When you may not need one',['If you ship a full container every week on one lane, you may deal directly with a shipping line or negotiate a contract. For most others a forwarder gives better rates, fewer surprises and one point of contact.'])])
X('how-to-choose-a-freight-forwarder',[('Checklist for comparing forwarders',['Same quote basis: door to door, or port to port, with the same Incoterm.','Same cargo details: weight, volume, packing, dangerous or not.','Transit time and sailing frequency as well as price.','Customs licence, insurance and how claims are handled.','References from shippers of similar cargo.']),('Start small',['If you are changing forwarder, try one shipment first and see how the desk handles the documents, the updates and a problem. The way a forwarder behaves when something goes wrong tells you more than the quote.'])])
X('customs-broker-role-and-licence',[('Checklist before you appoint a broker',['Licence number and the customs location it covers.','Name of the authorised person who will sign for your cargo.','Written scope: what is included in the fee and what is charged extra.','How and when you will be told the duty before the cargo moves.','The broker’s record at the stations where your cargo lands.']),('Your own responsibility',['A broker files on your behalf, but the declaration is yours. Read what is filed in your name, keep the documents the law asks you to keep, and tell the broker anything that affects value or classification, such as royalties or related-party pricing.'])])
X('how-to-import-into-india-step-by-step',[('Checklist for your first import',['IEC, GST and bank account ready.','Product classified and the duty and permissions confirmed.','Supplier agrees the Incoterm, price and documents.','Payment route agreed through an authorised dealer bank.','Broker, forwarder and delivery plan in place before the ship leaves.']),('After clearance',['Check the final bill of entry and keep it. You need it for GST input credit and for accounts. Compare the landed cost with your estimate, so the next order is priced better. Our <a href="landed-cost-calculator" style="color:#0A6CC2">landed cost calculator</a> helps with that.'])])
X('bill-of-entry-explained',[('Checklist before the bill is filed',['IEC and GST details match the invoice.','Description and HS code agree with the product literature.','Value includes freight, insurance and any royalty or assist.','Country of origin and any trade agreement claim are supported.','Permissions and registrations are attached.']),('When a bill is queried',['A query asks for a document or an explanation. Reply with exactly what is asked, and attach proof. A clear, quick reply usually closes it. A vague one invites more questions and more days.'])])
X('how-customs-duty-is-calculated-in-india',[('Checklist to work it out yourself',['Find the 8 digit HS code of the product.','Look up the basic duty rate and any exemption notification.','Work out the assessable value, including freight and insurance.','Add the surcharge on the duty and then IGST on the total.','Check for anti-dumping, safeguard or other duty on the product.']),('Why estimates differ from the final bill',['Exchange rates are fixed by Customs for the week and can differ from the bank rate. The value can be changed by the officer. And rates can change between your estimate and the filing. Use the estimate for planning, and ask your broker to confirm before you commit.'])])
X('air-freight-chargeable-weight-and-rates',[('Checklist before you ask for a rate',['Measure each carton or pallet, with packing, in centimetres.','Weigh each piece, with packing, in kilograms.','Work out the chargeable weight yourself so you can check the quote.','Say whether the cargo is general, perishable or dangerous.','State the cut-off date you must meet.']),('Rate types you may meet',['A general cargo rate per kg with weight breaks, so the rate per kg falls as the weight rises. A minimum charge for very small shipments. A specific commodity rate on some lanes. Ask which applies to yours and where the next break is, because paying for a few extra kilos can lower the total.'])])
X('air-freight-booking-steps',[('Checklist for a smooth booking',['Cargo ready, packed and labelled before the pickup.','Invoice, packing list and airway bill details agreed.','Export clearance planned to finish before the airline cut-off.','Consignee details and import clearance plan confirmed.','Tracking number shared with the buyer.']),('What to do if the flight is rolled',['Ask the forwarder for the next available flight and whether the cost changes. If the cargo is urgent, ask about a different airline or routing. Keep the buyer informed, since a rolled flight is the commonest reason for a missed delivery date.'])])
X('air-freight-vs-sea-freight',[('Checklist for the decision',['Value per kg of the goods against the freight cost per kg.','How long you can wait, and the cost of waiting.','Shelf life, fragility and the risk of damage.','Volume: a large shipment may suit sea even if urgent.','Whether part can go by air and the rest by sea.']),('A rule of thumb',['High value, light and urgent goes by air. Low value, heavy and not urgent goes by sea. Between the two, work the landed cost for each, include the cost of money in stock and the cost of a stock-out, and let the numbers decide.'])])
X('volumetric-weight-air-freight',[('Checklist to avoid paying for air',['Measure the outer carton, not the product inside it.','Round each side up to the next centimetre.','Remove empty space and oversize packing.','Compare the actual and volumetric weight for each piece.','Ask the carrier which divisor it uses.']),('Common error',['Measuring a pallet without the overhang or the stretch wrap, then being charged for the real dimensions at the airport. Measure what will actually be tendered.'])])
X('fcl-vs-lcl-shipping',[('Checklist for choosing',['Total volume in cubic metres and weight in tonnes.','Quotes for FCL and LCL on the same lane and Incoterm.','Delivery date and whether waiting for consolidation is acceptable.','Value and fragility of the cargo.','Where it will be cleared: port, CFS or an inland depot.']),('Rule of thumb',['Once LCL volume reaches a large share of a 20 ft container, the FCL quote is often close, and the cargo is handled less. Ask for both before you decide.'])])
X('ocean-freight-surcharges-explained',[('Checklist for your next quote',['Is the rate all-in or base plus surcharges?','Which currency is it in and which exchange rate applies?','Are the origin and destination charges included?','What are the free days and the detention tariff?','What happens if the booking is rolled or the port changes?']),('Why surcharges change',['Fuel cost, port congestion and demand all move. A surcharge that is announced after you book may or may not apply to your booking, so ask the forwarder and keep the answer in writing.'])])
X('delhi-ncr-icds-tughlakabad-dadri-patparganj',[('Checklist for choosing a depot',['Distance from the depot to your factory by truck.','Which depot the shipping line or rail operator serves from your port.','Rail transit time and frequency for your lane.','Depot charges, storage and free time.','Whether your broker is registered and active at that location.']),('Plan for the last mile',['Book the truck before the container reaches the depot, and know the depot’s gate hours and any restriction on vehicles. A container that waits for a truck at an inland depot costs money every day.'])])
X('mundra-port-guide',[('Checklist for cargo at Mundra',['Shipping line and terminal for your container confirmed.','Bill of entry filed before arrival for imports.','Truck or rail booked for the move out.','Export container: gate-in before the cut-off, with documents ready.','Free time and detention days noted.']),('Seasonal note',['Congestion and truck availability change with season and with the vessel schedule. Ask your forwarder what the situation is the week you ship, not what it was last quarter.'])])
X('jnpt-nhava-sheva-port-guide',[('Checklist for cargo at Nhava Sheva',['Terminal, line and free days confirmed.','Advance bill of entry for imports.','Choice between direct port delivery, CFS and inland depot decided.','Truck booking and gate timings.','Export cut-off and the documents for gate-in.']),('Planning the inland leg',['Cargo bound for north India may move by rail to Dadri or Tughlakabad, so decide before the ship arrives and ask your forwarder to align the rail booking with the vessel.'])])
X('mundra-vs-jnpt-which-port',[('Checklist for the comparison',['Total landed cost on both routes, not just ocean freight.','Rail and road legs and their reliability.','Shipping lines and frequency of sailings.','Port charges, free days and typical dwell time.','Your broker’s presence and experience at each port.']),('Mixed approach',['Some shippers use both, choosing the port by the shipment and the season. That is a valid answer: the best port for one shipment is not always the best for the next.'])])
X('icd-vs-cfs-vs-port-explained',[('Checklist for the choice',['LCL or FCL?','Distance of the factory from the port and from an inland depot.','Free days and storage cost at each place.','Rail connection and schedule.','Speed needed against cost.']),('Ask for the full cost',['Request a quote that adds the rail or road, the handling and the storage for each option, so you compare the total instead of one line. The cheapest line is not always the cheapest route.'])])
X('how-to-export-from-india-step-by-step',[('Checklist before the first export',['IEC, GST and bank account ready, and RCMC if you want benefits from an export promotion council.','Product classified, any export licence or restriction checked.','Buyer confirmed, order and payment terms agreed.','Packing, marking and labelling meet the destination rules.','Broker and forwarder briefed, and the shipping bill planned.']),('Know the destination rules',['The importing country’s rules decide what you must label, test and certify. Read our guides for the <a href="guides/exporting-to-the-usa-isf-10-2" style="color:#0A6CC2">USA</a>, <a href="guides/exporting-to-the-european-union" style="color:#0A6CC2">EU</a> and <a href="guides/exporting-to-the-uae" style="color:#0A6CC2">UAE</a>, and ask the buyer for the local requirements in writing.'])])
X('shipping-bill-explained',[('Checklist before you file',['Invoice, packing list and any certificate ready.','HS code, quantity and value consistent across all documents.','Scheme code selected: drawback, RoDTEP or none.','Port of export and destination country correct.','Container and seal details planned.']),('After the let export order',['Keep the shipping bill and the bill of lading together. Drawback, RoDTEP and the GST refund all use them, and so does the bank for realisation. A shipping bill that cannot be found later is money lost.'])])
X('documents-required-for-import-into-india',[('Checklist of the core set',['Commercial invoice and packing list.','Bill of lading or airway bill.','Bill of entry, filed by your broker.','IEC and GST registration of the importer.','Certificate of origin if you claim a trade agreement rate.','Licences, certificates and test reports for regulated goods.']),('Keep your records',['Keep import documents for the period the law requires, since Customs can ask for them after clearance. Store the scans together with the bill of entry and the payment proof.'])])
X('hs-code-classification-general-rules',[('Checklist to classify a product',['Write a full description: material, use, how it is made.','Find the heading by the text and notes of the Tariff.','Apply the general rules in order.','Check the national eight digit code and its rate.','Record why you chose it, and keep the supporting data.']),('When to ask for help',['If two codes seem to fit, if the rate difference is large or if the product is new, ask a broker or seek a ruling. The cost of asking is small against a demand notice later.'])])
X('demurrage-and-detention-explained',[('Checklist to stay out of demurrage',['Know the free days for the port and for the container.','File the bill of entry before the vessel arrives.','Pre-book the truck or rail slot.','Plan the empty return so detention does not start.','Watch for holidays and strikes that can eat the free days.']),('Disputes',['If a charge looks wrong, ask the line or terminal for the breakdown. Keep the gate-in and gate-out times and the correspondence, because a waiver depends on proof of who caused the delay.'])])
X('bill-of-lading-explained',[('Checklist when the bill is issued',['Check the draft as soon as you get it.','Confirm freight terms and the notify party.','Agree the number of originals and who receives them.','Confirm whether it is original, telex release or sea waybill.','Keep a copy with the invoice and the packing list.']),('Types you may meet',['Original bills of lading, telex released and sea waybills each work differently. Use the original when the bank needs it, and a telex release or a waybill when the parties trust each other and want speed.'])])
X('airway-bill-mawb-hawb-explained',[('Checklist when the airway bill is issued',['Shipper and consignee match the invoice.','Pieces, weight and chargeable weight are right.','Airports and flight details are right.','Freight prepaid or collect is as agreed.','Description of goods and the special handling codes are right.']),('Reading status updates',['A booking, receipt, departure, arrival and delivery each appear as a status code. If a status does not change for a day, ask your forwarder to check with the airline, because a shipment can wait at a transit airport for the next flight.'])])
X('import-export-code-iec',[('Checklist for the application',['PAN of the business, and Aadhaar or digital signature of the signatory.','Bank account proof in the same name.','Address proof of the business premises.','Email and mobile number that you control.','A plan for the annual update.']),('Tip',['Keep the IEC certificate, the PAN, GST and bank details in one folder. Your broker and your bank will ask for them again and again.'])])
X('express-courier-vs-air-freight',[('Checklist for choosing',['Weight and size of the consignment.','Whether door-to-door delivery is needed.','Value and the customs rules for it.','Delivery date and tracking needs.','Cost of each at your actual chargeable weight.']),('Ask for both',['Get a courier quote and an air freight quote for the same cargo. For small parcels the courier is often the easier answer, and as weight grows the airfreight rate usually wins.'])])
X('container-types-explained',[('Checklist to choose a container',['Cargo dimensions, weight and packing type.','Need for temperature control, ventilation or open access.','Payload limit of the container against your cargo weight.','Loading and unloading facilities at both ends.','Cost per container against cost per unit of cargo.']),('Before you load',['Check the container is clean, dry and free of damage and smell, take photographs, record the seal number and mark the cargo clearly. Our <a href="guides/container-seals-and-numbers" style="color:#0A6CC2">guide to seals and numbers</a> explains what to record.'])])
X('customs-examination-and-out-of-charge',[('Checklist for an examination',['Broker or authorised person present.','Invoice, packing list and certificates at hand.','Cargo accessible and labelled.','Labour and handling arranged.','Samples and test requirements understood.']),('After release',['Keep the out of charge copy with the bill of entry and the duty payment. Check the delivery order, pay the depot charges and move the cargo before the free days end.'])])
X('bis-certification-for-imports',[('Checklist for BIS cargo',['Confirm that the product is under compulsory registration.','Check whether the overseas factory holds a valid registration.','Get the registration number and the mark on the label.','Allow time for lab testing and registration for a new supplier.','Give your broker the certificate before the cargo ships.']),('If the cargo has no BIS',['Do not wait for it to arrive. Ask your broker what options exist, and expect delay and cost. The cheapest fix is always before shipping.'])])
